= Example events <app-examples>

`examples/canonical.jsonl` holds one event per observable in the catalogue (plus both edges of `TookSnapshot`), in canonical form. It validates against `schema/observables.schema.json`.

*Provenance.* Every line is a real event from a Haskell node's log (`log-node-10.jsonl`, a 6-node workbench cluster run, September 2026), not a hand-written example. Lines were taken unchanged, except for these normalisations to canonical form, each one a documented deviation (@sec-deviations):

#table(
  columns: (1fr, auto),
  table.header[Normalisation][Deviation],
  [Points at genesis: `"genesis (origin)"` → `"genesis"`], [S1],
  [`TookSnapshot.tip`: `"RealPoint (SlotNo n) <hash>"` → `"<hash>@n"`], [S2],
  [ChainHash at genesis: `"GenesisHash"` / `"Genesis"` → `"genesis"`], [S3, S4],
  [`BlockContext`: `"current slot"` → `slot`, `tipBlockNo` → `blockNo`, `tip` → `prev`], [S5, S6, S7],
  [`Mempool.*`: the optional `tx` / `txs` fields are removed. The log only holds truncated TxIds, and full ones can't be reconstructed from it.], [S8],
)

To keep the lines short, unconsumed fields were removed as well: `newSuffixSelectView` / `oldSuffixSelectView` of the `ChainDB.AddBlockEvent.*` events, and `tip` of `ChainSync.ServerHeader.Update`. Unknown fields are allowed (@sec-envelope-fields).
